    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1940783824729760190",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1940783824729760190",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1940783824729760190",
      "text": "[3:30PM] #AlausaIkeja #TrafficUpdate \n\nSteady movement is observed on Obafemi Awolowo Way, starting from the Coca-Cola junction, proceeding through Radio and Allen junctions, with traffic becoming busy around Balogun Street as vehicles approach the Olowu area due to significant turning activity.\n\n From Olowu towards the underpass, traffic flow is steady. On Lateef Jakande Road, movement is fast from the Coca-Cola junction, passing LTV8 and Daily Times, with increased activity near Cadbury due to alternation delays. \n\n Beyond Cadbury, traffic is also picking up speed towards the Omole roundabout. Aromire Street is experiencing busy movement inbound Adeniyi and through to Akko Villa, though this is not currently causing alarm. \n\nMobolaji Johnson Avenue has good traffic flow along its entire stretch, from the old Tollgate and 7up gate through BillingsWay to the Alausa intersection. Lastly, the access points to and from Dr. Nurudeen Olowopopo Drive connecting to Otedola under the bridge are also reporting good traffic flow. \n\nNo impediments have been observed, and personnel remain on standby to address any traffic issues. \n\n#FollowLASTMA",
