    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1940793080153612435",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1940793080153612435",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1940793080153612435",
      "text": "[4:06PM] #EbuteEro #Apongbon #trafficUpdate \n\n The CMS bridge towards the Offin Canal market is experiencing slow movement due to a high volume of vehicles, ongoing market activities, and frequent vehicular ingress and egress at the market. However, immediately after the Offin Canal market, the stretch leading to Ijora Olopa by the NEPA intersection is flowing well.\n\n Broad Street from the Apongbon underpass, connecting to the Offin Canal market and Olowogbowo, is also experiencing slow but steady movement due to market activities and the evening rush hour. Conversely, Eko Bridge by the NEPA intersection heading inward Apongbon reports good traffic flow. \n\nThe descent from Eko Bridge inward towards CMS, passing Elegbeta Mini Stadium and connecting to the Ebute-Ero market, shows steady movement, with traffic from the Ebute-Ero exit also flowing smoothly towards Eko Bridge. \n\nFurthermore, the Ebute-Ero market route inbound to Leventist, via the UBA roundabout, and connecting to both inner and outer Marina, is also reporting good traffic flow. Currently, no major impediments have been reported, and personnel are visibly present to manage the traffic situation.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
